  m_Name: Note_SignalDiscovery2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  title: 'Communication Tool '
  key: 25
  topic: 2
  boardContentText: The lighthouse is a communication tool
  boardSprite: {fileID: 0}
  contentText: "Date: [faded]\n\nFollowing the most recent measurements, I am confirming
    the conclusion I have long been reluctant to record: the lighthouse is not a
    sensory device. Nor is it a modifier of the environment. It is a communication
    tool.\n\nThe beam patterns we transmit produce responses that cannot be explained
    physically. The responses have structure. Sequence. Logic. Something down there
    understands. Something \u2014 answers.\n\nThe team refuses to enter this into
    the official protocol. Smith stays silent. Blum runs. Kellerstein hasn't worked
    in a long time \u2014 he walks the island back and forth, as if he's gone mad.
    He talks to himself. I avoid him.\n\nOnly I can see what we have before us.\n\nAnd
    I see more.\n\nWhen I transmitted a pattern yesterday that I had been testing
    in silence, off the schedule... the water pulled back. And beneath it, I saw
    Anton.\n\nHe's standing there. Beneath the water. My brother.\n\nI know how this
    sounds. I know that if anyone read this, they would have me before a psychiatric
    commission before sunset. I know.\n\nBut it is him. I am not mistaken. Anton
    stands down there. Waiting.\n\nThis work has long ceased to be about oceanography.\nIt
    is about who we are speaking to.\nAnd whether we can bring him back.\n\n\u2014
    H. Vogel"
  paperSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cea3c49c6ad23de4286197f5004fc48e, type: 3}
